Menu="NetworkServices"
Title="Folevi Server"
Icon="folevi.png"
---
<?php
$cfg = parse_ini_file("/boot/config/plugins/folevi/folevi.cfg") ?: parse_ini_file("/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/folevi/default.cfg");
$running = trim(shell_exec("/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/folevi/scripts/rc.folevi status")) === "running";
$port = htmlspecialchars($cfg['FOLEVI_PORT'] ?? '8460');
?>
<p>Folevi Server is <strong><?= $running ? "running" : "stopped" ?></strong>.
<?php if ($running): ?>
<a href="http://<?= htmlspecialchars($_SERVER['SERVER_NAME'] ?? 'tower') ?>:<?= $port ?>/" target="_blank">Open Folevi Server</a>
<?php endif; ?></p>

<form markdown="1" method="POST" action="/update.php" target="progressFrame">
<input type="hidden" name="#file" value="folevi/folevi.cfg">
<input type="hidden" name="#command" value="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/folevi/scripts/rc.folevi">
<input type="hidden" name="#arg[1]" value="restart">

Start with the array:
: <select name="AUTOSTART">
  <?= mk_option($cfg['AUTOSTART'] ?? 'yes', "yes", "Yes") ?>
  <?= mk_option($cfg['AUTOSTART'] ?? 'yes', "no", "No") ?>
  </select>

Data folder:
: <input type="text" name="DATA_DIR" value="<?= htmlspecialchars($cfg['DATA_DIR']) ?>" class="narrow">

> Everyone's notes and files live here. A pool path (for example /mnt/cache/appdata/folevi/data) is best for the database.

Program folder:
: <input type="text" name="INSTALL_DIR" value="<?= htmlspecialchars($cfg['INSTALL_DIR']) ?>" class="narrow">

Port (HTTP):
: <input type="number" name="FOLEVI_PORT" value="<?= $port ?>" class="narrow">

Port (HTTPS):
: <input type="number" name="FOLEVI_HTTPS_PORT" value="<?= htmlspecialchars($cfg['FOLEVI_HTTPS_PORT'] ?? '8443') ?>" class="narrow">

Run as user:
: <input type="text" name="RUN_AS" value="<?= htmlspecialchars($cfg['RUN_AS'] ?? 'nobody') ?>" class="narrow">

&nbsp;
: <input type="submit" value="Apply and restart"><input type="button" value="Done" onclick="done()">
</form>
